# What `vercel deploy` uploads from this checkout (R-61). The Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore: without this file it uploaded
# 52,671 files, the root .env, the test screenshots and the old static export among them. So every rule git has is listed again here.
# `vercel deploy --prebuilt` ignores this file (it uploads only .vercel/output).
# One deliberate difference from .gitignore: web/.og-cache (the Commons thumbnail cache scripts/images.mjs and scripts/og.mjs read)
# is uploaded, so a build from this Mac does not fetch about 300 photos again. A git-connected build never has it.
# Also uploaded: web/.generated/legacy-trips.json, the trip list tools/hub.py derives from the frozen legacy pages, so the build does
# not depend on python3 being on the build machine.

# Secrets: never upload
.env
.env.*
*.local.json
.neon
.vercel
.claude/settings.local.json

# Dependencies, caches and build output (rebuilt on Vercel)
node_modules
.next
.site
.wrangler
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
tools/.cache
web/out
web/.next
web/.generated/*
!web/.generated/legacy-trips.json
web/.fixture-*
web/.tile-cache
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/shots
web/public/img
web/public/og
web/next-env.d.ts
web/AGENTS.md
*.tsbuildinfo

# Regenerable local files
.DS_Store
*.swp
*-candidates.json
links-report.txt
legacy/_system/gallery.html

# Never read by the build or a server function (anchored: core/test has a fixture folder named research)
/docs
/research
/.claude
